#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Observation]
#title[Groupoid Cardinality agrees with set cardinality]

Let $X : "1-Type"$. If $X$ is a finite set, then its groupoid cardinality is well-defined and agrees with the usual cardinality of finite sets.

#proof[
  Since $X$ is a set it is equivalent to its set truncation. Since $X$ is finite $X$ is automatically $pi_0$-finite.
  Since $X$ is a set its #local("00H6")[automorphism group] is trivial everywhere. Therefor
  $
    |X|_"groupoid" -= plus.big_(c : ||X||_0) 1/(|"Aut"_X (c)|) = plus.big_(c : ||X||_0) 1 = plus.big_(x : X) 1= |X|.
  $
]

This justifies using the same notation for both groupoid and set cardinality.

